---
/**
 * Local test harness for the STL viewer plugin.
 *
 * Not linked from any nav — visit /stl-test directly.
 *
 * Validates:
 *   - Multiple viewers on one page (only first should auto-load on view).
 *   - All material variants.
 *   - All height tokens.
 *   - Responsive grid collapse at narrow widths.
 *   - In-content placement matching real article layout.
 *   - Lazy loading — viewers below the fold stay as placeholders until scrolled.
 */
import StlViewer from "emdash-plugin-stl-viewer/astro/StlViewer.astro";
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";

const fixtures = {
	cube: "/stls/cube.stl",
	icos: "/stls/icosahedron.stl",
	torus: "/stls/torus.stl",
	knurled: "/stls/knurled.stl",
	cube3mf: "/stls/cube.3mf",
	icos3mf: "/stls/icosahedron.3mf",
	torus3mf: "/stls/torus.3mf",
};
---

<Base title="STL Viewer Test" description="Local test harness for the STL plugin">
	<div class="page">
		<header class="page-head">
			<span class="page-eyebrow">internal · test</span>
			<h1>STL Viewer test bench</h1>
			<p class="page-lede">
				Each viewer below initializes its 3D scene only when scrolled near, so
				the page itself stays light. Three.js is shared across viewers — the
				library loads once.
			</p>
		</header>

		<section class="block">
			<h2>1. Article-width placement</h2>
			<p>
				This mirrors how a viewer looks embedded in a blog post. Same column
				width as <code>/posts/*</code>, with surrounding prose for context.
			</p>
			<div class="article-like">
				<p>
					When I designed this part, I went through several iterations to get
					the wall thickness right. The first version flexed too much under
					load, the second was too heavy to print quickly.
				</p>
				<StlViewer
					node={{
						id: fixtures.knurled,
						title: "Knurled grip — v3",
						caption: "Final revision. 96-segment ridges, 2mm draft.",
						material: "matte",
						color: "#cfd1d4",
						height: "standard",
						autoRotate: true,
						showGrid: true,
					}}
				/>
				<p>
					Drag to orbit, scroll to zoom. The auto-rotation pauses while you're
					interacting and resumes after a few seconds of idle.
				</p>
			</div>
		</section>

		<section class="block">
			<h2>2. Material variants</h2>
			<p>All five materials, same geometry, rendered side-by-side.</p>
			<div class="grid grid-3">
				<StlViewer
					node={{
						id: fixtures.icos,
						title: "Matte",
						material: "matte",
						color: "#cfd1d4",
						height: "compact",
					}}
				/>
				<StlViewer
					node={{
						id: fixtures.icos,
						title: "Glossy",
						material: "glossy",
						color: "#22d3ee",
						height: "compact",
					}}
				/>
				<StlViewer
					node={{
						id: fixtures.icos,
						title: "Metal",
						material: "metal",
						color: "#d4d4d8",
						height: "compact",
					}}
				/>
				<StlViewer
					node={{
						id: fixtures.icos,
						title: "Clay (unlit)",
						material: "clay",
						color: "#e7c89c",
						height: "compact",
					}}
				/>
				<StlViewer
					node={{
						id: fixtures.icos,
						title: "Normal map",
						material: "normal",
						height: "compact",
					}}
				/>
				<StlViewer
					node={{
						id: fixtures.icos,
						title: "No grid",
						material: "matte",
						color: "#f59e0b",
						height: "compact",
						showGrid: false,
						autoRotate: false,
					}}
				/>
			</div>
		</section>

		<section class="block">
			<h2>3. Heights</h2>
			<div class="grid grid-3">
				<StlViewer
					node={{
						id: fixtures.cube,
						title: "Compact (320px)",
						material: "matte",
						color: "#22d3ee",
						height: "compact",
					}}
				/>
				<StlViewer
					node={{
						id: fixtures.cube,
						title: "Standard (440px)",
						material: "matte",
						color: "#22d3ee",
						height: "standard",
					}}
				/>
				<StlViewer
					node={{
						id: fixtures.cube,
						title: "Tall (560px)",
						material: "matte",
						color: "#22d3ee",
						height: "tall",
					}}
				/>
			</div>
		</section>

		<section class="block">
			<h2>4. Complex mesh (3,072 triangles)</h2>
			<p>
				A torus with finer tessellation, to check normals and rotation handling
				on a non-trivial mesh.
			</p>
			<StlViewer
				node={{
					id: fixtures.torus,
					title: "Torus",
					material: "glossy",
					color: "#22d3ee",
					height: "tall",
					showGrid: true,
				}}
			/>
		</section>

		<section class="block">
			<h2>5. Broken URL (error state)</h2>
			<StlViewer
				node={{
					id: "/stls/does-not-exist.stl",
					title: "404 model",
					material: "matte",
					color: "#cfd1d4",
					height: "compact",
				}}
			/>
		</section>

		<section class="block">
			<h2>6. 3MF format (auto-detected by extension)</h2>
			<p>
				Same primitives as the STL grid above, but stored as zipped 3MF.
				The 3MF loader downloads lazily on first 3MF viewer (adds ~50 KB
				including fflate; STL-only pages don't pay for it).
			</p>
			<div class="grid grid-3">
				<StlViewer
					node={{
						id: fixtures.cube3mf,
						title: "Cube — 3MF",
						material: "matte",
						color: "#22d3ee",
						height: "compact",
					}}
				/>
				<StlViewer
					node={{
						id: fixtures.icos3mf,
						title: "Icosahedron — 3MF",
						material: "glossy",
						color: "#fbbf24",
						height: "compact",
					}}
				/>
				<StlViewer
					node={{
						id: fixtures.torus3mf,
						title: "Torus — 3MF",
						material: "metal",
						color: "#d4d4d8",
						height: "compact",
					}}
				/>
			</div>
		</section>

		<section class="block">
			<h2>7. 3MF with explicit format override</h2>
			<p>
				URL without extension — `format: "3mf"` tells the viewer which loader
				to use.
			</p>
			<StlViewer
				node={{
					id: "/stls/cube.3mf",
					title: "Forced 3MF",
					material: "clay",
					color: "#e7c89c",
					height: "standard",
					format: "3mf",
				}}
			/>
		</section>

		<section class="block">
			<h2>8. Lazy load check (far below)</h2>
			<p style="min-height: 1400px; padding-top: 32px; color: var(--color-muted);">
				The viewer below should remain a placeholder until you scroll to it,
				then load on its own. Three.js does not download until the first viewer
				on the page is loaded.
			</p>
			<StlViewer
				node={{
					id: fixtures.cube,
					title: "Loaded only on demand",
					material: "metal",
					color: "#22d3ee",
					height: "standard",
				}}
			/>
		</section>
	</div>
</Base>

<style>
	.page {
		max-width: var(--wide-width);
		margin: 0 auto;
		padding: var(--spacing-10) var(--spacing-6) var(--spacing-16);
	}

	.page-head {
		margin-bottom: var(--spacing-12);
		padding-bottom: var(--spacing-8);
		border-bottom: 1px solid var(--color-border-subtle);
	}

	.page-eyebrow {
		display: inline-block;
		font-family: var(--font-mono);
		font-size: 0.7rem;
		letter-spacing: 0.12em;
		text-transform: uppercase;
		color: var(--color-muted);
		margin-bottom: var(--spacing-3);
	}

	.page-head h1 {
		font-family: var(--font-serif);
		font-size: var(--font-size-4xl);
		font-weight: 400;
		font-style: italic;
		letter-spacing: -0.01em;
		margin-bottom: var(--spacing-3);
	}

	.page-lede {
		font-family: var(--font-serif);
		font-size: var(--font-size-lg);
		line-height: var(--leading-relaxed);
		color: var(--color-text-secondary);
		max-width: 60ch;
	}

	.block {
		margin: var(--spacing-12) 0;
	}

	.block h2 {
		font-family: var(--font-serif);
		font-size: var(--font-size-2xl);
		font-weight: 400;
		margin-bottom: var(--spacing-3);
	}

	.block p {
		font-family: var(--font-serif);
		font-size: var(--font-size-base);
		color: var(--color-text-secondary);
		line-height: var(--leading-relaxed);
		max-width: 70ch;
		margin-bottom: var(--spacing-4);
	}

	.block code {
		font-family: var(--font-mono);
		font-size: 0.85em;
		background: var(--color-surface);
		padding: 0.15em 0.35em;
		border-radius: var(--radius);
	}

	.article-like {
		max-width: var(--content-width);
		margin: 0 auto;
		font-family: var(--font-serif);
		font-size: var(--font-size-lg);
		line-height: 1.8;
		color: var(--color-text);
	}

	.article-like p {
		font-size: var(--font-size-lg);
		color: var(--color-text);
		margin-bottom: 1.5em;
		max-width: none;
	}

	.grid {
		display: grid;
		gap: var(--spacing-6);
	}

	.grid-3 {
		grid-template-columns: repeat(3, minmax(0, 1fr));
	}

	@media (max-width: 1024px) {
		.grid-3 {
			grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr));
		}
	}

	@media (max-width: 640px) {
		.grid-3 {
			grid-template-columns: 1fr;
		}
		.page {
			padding: var(--spacing-6) var(--spacing-4);
		}
		.page-head h1 {
			font-size: var(--font-size-3xl);
		}
	}
</style>
